From af838ba977cf97324d0ab2c8d6fbf32fb003ab74 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 06:46:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/18] feat(controller): check deployed instances periodically

Instances were only checked once, when the control plane started, so
an instance that exited while the control plane kept running stayed
behind a Ready service: the gateway kept routing to it and nothing
redeployed it.

The controller manager now takes an optional instance check and runs
it every instance_check_interval seconds, next to the change poll and
the resync, queueing the services it reports. The application binds
check_instances to its registry and launcher, so a lost instance turns
its service Degraded at the next check and the reconciler redeploys it
with the existing backoff; a Degraded service whose instance is back
is reported and returns to Ready. A failing check is logged and
retried at the next interval, and stopping the manager cancels it.

FORGEMESH_INSTANCE_CHECK_INTERVAL_SECONDS sets the interval (default
10 seconds) and must be a finite positive number; the application
validates it even without a launcher so that a typo does not go
unnoticed. The check only asks the launcher whether the instance runs:
verify() is the launch readiness wait of the process launchers, not a
cheap probe, so a hung but alive process is not detected.
